                {
                  "id": "guide-a-t",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Opt for financing when your plan calls for ownership, equity build-up, and long-term asset value.\n\nConsider leasing if you prefer lower upfront costs, predictable payments, and the option to refresh your truck periodically.\n\nChoose a direct lease when you want to align payments to usage, seasonality, or business cycles.\n\nSelect our semi-truck leasing model for added flexibility in fleet composition and a partnership that adapts as your business evolves.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "guide-b",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 6
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "guide-b-h",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Questions businesses typically face",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "guide-b-t",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What monthly payments make sense for your ROI and cash flow?\n\nDo you want to own the truck when the term ends, or prefer to return and refresh under lease?\n\nWhat are the residual values and tax implications of a lease vs. financing?\n\nHow can you gain the flexibility of semi-truck leasing while aligning your fleet with seasonal demand or growth plans?",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
